                <pb facs="1207" n="1095" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg1095"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1123 Winterle/14: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-10-07T15:00:00+08:00">October 7, 1935—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 7—10:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>84. Embassy’s October 3, 11 a.m.<anchor n="91" xml:id="d1053-f1"/> and previous.
                    In view of the statement made by Paxton in his October 1, 8 p.m., repeated in my
                    October 2, 3 p.m., that he is satisfied that Navy was involved, I am instructing
                    Paxton to return to Chefoo. He will propose to the Japanese Consul in view of
                    the conflicting reports telegraphed regarding the origin of the affray and the
                    difficulty of arriving at the facts that unless he after consideration has
                    further suggestions for means of arriving at the facts or unless he desires to
                    await outcome Winterle case, either, (1) the case be dropped with mutual oral
                    assurances to make efforts to prevent disturbances involving their respective
                    nationals or, (2), mutual regrets be orally expressed for any participation by
                    police officers and naval personnel that may have occurred with mutual
                    assurances investigation under (1).</p>
                <p>I am instructing Ballantine to remain here pending outcome of this proposal but
                    consider it advisable that he visit Chefoo later irrespective of whether
                    proposal is accepted.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
